In the images/ directory on disc1, there are two img files.  You need to
put those images onto respective floppies using dd in unix or rawrite in
windows.  In the milo/images/ directory, you need gunzip the sx164.img.gz
file and put that file onto floppy. 

You need to configure the AlphaBIOS to boot off of the milo floppy.
Once you get the "MILO>" prompt, type "fd0:" to initialize the floppy
drive.  Insert the generic.img floppy and type "boot".  You'll eventually
be prompted for the ramdisk.img floppy.  You can even type in "boot text
expert", I think.  


