Michal,

Thank you for all of this information.  I wanted to use Red Hat 7.2 but could
not find the updates and was worried about getting quick updates for security
problems, etc.  I have reinstalled 7.2 on our system and am currently trying
to get RAID-1 to work.  Looks like we will need to recompile the kernel with
RAID-1 support.

It appears that our strange problems were because os_type was not set to UNIX
in the SRM.  Setting it to UNIX appears to bypass AlphaBIOS and things are
working much better now, using aboot.  Now Linux sees the two processors and
none of the other errors have appeared... yet.

