I've seen this before when the machine isn't actually hung.  If you don't have the CONFIG_VT_CONSOLE 
config option on (under Character devices) in that kernel build, you won't see anything on the 
screen, but it will boot.

After it gets to this point, do you see any disk access?  Can you ping the machine after a few 
minutes?  If so, you probably need a new kernel with that option enabled.  Otherwise, you may want 
to see if you have the same type of cpu now as you did before.  If not, build a new kernel for that 
cpu or Generic and try it.

