Soterro wrote:
> Hello,
> 
> I cannot start the installation of the thing on a Digital Personal
> Workstation 500a. I used the software downloaded from debian (their
> 3.0 release), so the floppy called milo_alcor.bin

I don't think you have the correct MILO image; Personal Workstation 500a 
is not of the type alcor, but of the type miata, as far as I know (and I 
should, because I'm running an PWS433au).

If you wish to run Debian on such a machine (as I do :-)), I consider it 
a much easier way to get rid of AlphaBIOS, and use SRM (that is the 
other one of the two options you can choose in your bootrom -- 
appearantly it is now set to AlphaBIOS on your system).
Once you have SRM, you don't need MILO anymore, and the bootloader that 
Debian's setup will install for you is called aboot. Now this is an easy 
to configure bootloader if I ever saw one!
I'm not sure which menu to choose within AlphBIOS to get it set to SRM, 
but it's fairly easy. Just check out all the possible options. It might 
not be called SRM as such, it might be called 'unix' or something :-)

Also, see the faq on this stuff at www.alphalinux.org of 
www.linuxalpha.org or search in google.

Be sure to read Debian's installation instructions for Alpha as well, it 
on-line on their site. It is helpful.

Good luck,

Dannis.




