Most of the pci graphics card are supported by SRM by means of BIOS
emulation.
If you want to put a mac card, you should update the card rom to revert
it to intel support.
You'd better chose a card which is supported by linux/xfree combination.
In my opinion the best is ati radeon pci which works fot both 2d and 3d.
I haven't tried it yet :( but i'm now using a matrox g450 pci which is
damn good at 2d and video playback but has no opengl/dri support at all
(kernel dependecies to agp)

