Hello. I've been working for a while on a patch to the linux kernel
that implements page coloring, and thought it was time to announce to
a wider community. Patches are available here:

www.boo.net/~jasonp/page_color-2.2.20-20020108.patch
www.boo.net/~jasonp/page_color-2.4.17-20020113.patch
www.boo.net/~jasonp/page_color-2.4.18-20020705.patch

All the different versions use the same basic algorithm. It's been
tested on alpha and (somewhat) on x86, and gives performance
improvements on both architectures (the code is architecture
independent). I'm told that the basic page coloring engine has been
incorporated into Andrea Arcangeli's 2.2.21 kernel.

Instructions for use are in the patch. I hope that it's in some way
useful, and would be happy to help with problems or questions. 

Thanks in advance,
jasonp

PS: For Alpha, page coloring can work together with Naohiko Shimizu's
super-page patch. I think the two patches solve complementary
problems, and so together can achieve high performance across a wider
range of codes.



