One problem you might be having is a bad SCSI connection.  Unplug the Alpha,
then open it up, and remove all the drives from the SCSI chain, boot this
way.  Turn it off, plug one drive in, then boot, going on until you have all
the drives back in.  This gives the machine time to sort out it differences
with the SCSI controller, and it should work in formating when you have all
the drives back in.  I had the same problem, but be sure to keep the Alpha
on for a long time to make sure it is not just going very slowly.

Jeremy

