>  I am setting it up with case/ps/drives/etc and wondered about PCI
> graphics cards. Will the Alpha use standard Intel PCI cards or is it
> different like the Mac PCI?
>

    It uses Intel PCI video cards BUT not all (and not many).  Alpha's are
very finicky with video cards.  You can check out www.linuxalpha.org and
find the compatibility list for you motherboard.  In my limited knowlodge of
hardware, Intel graphics cards use x86 code in the ROM.  For an Alpha
motherboard to use a video card with x86 code the firmware on the
motherboard (SRM or AlphaBIOS) has to emulate the code on the video card.
Hence, the limited video card support.

    Another tip is to use the SRM firmware with Alpha's if you can. IMHO it
is much better than AlphaBIOS.  I imagine you'll get a few more posts with
more info than I can offer.  Good Luck!




