On Mon, 01 Jul 2002 20:14:09 +0200, Werner Saar wrote:

> I installed Redhat 7.1 on a AlphaServer 800. This machine also has an
> Mylex DAC960P controller. The controller was not recognized by the
> Kernel 2.4.9.
> First I updatet the firmware of the DAC960P to version 2.73. After that
> I compiled Kernel 2.4.16 with support for DAC960 ( not as module ). At
> boot of kernel 2.4.16 , the Mylex controller is seen, but there is an
> error at initialization with unknown return-code FB

Just two hints:

- Try it with a 2.4.18 kernel. 2.x BIOS revisions on the DAC960 are
IIRC not supported with the driver included in 2.4.16.

- If your machine has lots of RAM try reducing it with the 'mem=' boot
option. The DAC960 driver has problems if the physical address range
exceeds 2GB.

hth, regards
  Michael Keller
