If you have your filesystem spread over multiple disks (which is what it
looks like you did), make sure the drives  (the scsi disks) are jumpered to
spin-up on power-on..   Usually they are set to start on command, however
only the boot disk would be started by the firmware. The others would remain
spun down.

JJ

